<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('partials/head') %>
  <style>
    .legal-body { background: var(--color-pearl); min-height: 100vh; }
    .legal-page { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 5rem; }
    .legal-back {
      display: inline-block; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.85rem;
      font-weight: 400; color: var(--color-bloem); text-decoration: none; margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }
    .legal-back:hover { opacity: 0.7; }
    .legal-title {
      font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 2.4rem; font-weight: 400;
      color: var(--color-ink-stained); margin: 0 0 0.4rem; line-height: 1.12;
    }
    .legal-updated {
      font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 300;
      color: rgba(16, 15, 16, 0.55); margin: 0 0 2.25rem;
    }
    .legal-page h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 400;
      color: var(--color-ink-stained); margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; line-height: 1.2;
    }
    .legal-page h3 {
      font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.98rem; font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--color-ink-stained); margin: 1.5rem 0 0.4rem;
    }
    .legal-page p, .legal-page li {
      font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 300;
      line-height: 1.7; color: rgba(16, 15, 16, 0.82);
    }
    .legal-page p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .legal-page ul { margin: 0 0 1rem; padding-left: 1.35rem; }
    .legal-page li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    .legal-page a { color: var(--color-bloem); text-underline-offset: 2px; }
    .legal-footer {
      margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(112, 92, 108, 0.15);
      font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 300; color: rgba(16, 15, 16, 0.5);
    }
    @media (max-width: 560px) { .legal-title { font-size: 1.9rem; } }
  </style>
</head>
<body class="legal-body">
  <main class="legal-page">
    <a href="/" class="legal-back">← Back</a>

    <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: July 12, 2026</p>

    <p>
      The Creative's Garden ("the platform," "we," "us") is a content-creation course
      run by The Meibos Touch (Julia Meibos). This policy explains what personal
      information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and the choices you
      have. We've written it in plain language on purpose.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      The platform is operated by The Meibos Touch. For privacy purposes, we act as the
      "data controller" for your information. If you have any questions about this policy
      or your data, email us at
      <a href="mailto:julia@meibostouch.com">julia@meibostouch.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <h3>Account &amp; profile</h3>
    <p>
      Your name, email address, and a securely hashed password. Optionally, a profile
      photo, your timezone, and the season you've chosen.
    </p>
    <h3>The things you create</h3>
    <p>
      The notes you log about your recordings, your weekly intentions and goals, your
      seed packets, and your answers to the opening and closing self-assessments.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Your daily videos stay with you.</strong> You record on your own device,
      and only log written notes here — we do not collect, upload, or store your video
      files.
    </p>
    <h3>Preferences</h3>
    <p>
      Your reminder settings and your community-visibility choices. If you turn on the
      newsletter or reminders, we record that consent.
    </p>
    <h3>Payment</h3>
    <p>
      If you purchase the paid course, your payment is handled by Stripe. We receive
      confirmation and limited billing details, but we never see or store your full
      card number.
    </p>
    <h3>Technical</h3>
    <p>
      A session cookie to keep you signed in; a device token if you enable push
      notifications; and basic server logs (such as IP address and timestamps) that
      help us keep the service secure and reliable.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To run the platform — your account, dashboard, goals, and community features.</li>
      <li>To sign you in and keep your account secure.</li>
      <li>To send service emails you need, like password resets, via Resend.</li>
      <li>To send the daily and weekly reminders you turn on, by email and/or push.</li>
      <li>If you opt in, to send you The Meibos Touch newsletter via Mailchimp.</li>
      <li>To process payments for the paid course, via Stripe.</li>
      <li>To understand what's working and improve the platform.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
    <p>
      The platform uses a single <strong>essential cookie</strong> to keep you signed
      in. It's required for the site to work and is not used for advertising or
      cross-site tracking. We do not run third-party advertising or analytics cookies on
      the site itself.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you click a link in one of our emails, our email tools (Mailchimp, and Google
      Analytics for campaign tracking) may record that click so we can understand
      engagement. You can avoid this by not clicking email links, and you can
      unsubscribe from marketing emails at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>Your private content</h2>
    <p>
      The notes and reflections you log are private to your account by default. The only
      things other students can see are the limited progress indicators you explicitly
      choose to share in your community settings — and you can change those anytime from
      your <a href="/profile">profile</a>. As your course facilitator, Julia may access
      account information to support you, while respecting the private nature of your
      practice.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information. We share limited data with the service
      providers that help us run the platform, each under their own privacy terms:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Railway</strong> — hosting and database (where your account and content live).</li>
      <li><strong>Resend</strong> — sending service and reminder emails.</li>
      <li><strong>Mailchimp</strong> — sending the newsletter and reminders you opt into.</li>
      <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — processing payments for the paid course.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — measuring clicks on links in our marketing emails.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may also disclose information if the law requires it, or to protect the safety
      and rights of our users.
    </p>

    <h2>Legal bases (for EU/UK users)</h2>
    <p>
      Where the GDPR applies, we rely on: performing our contract with you (to run your
      account and course); your consent (for the newsletter); and our legitimate
      interests (keeping the service secure and improving it). You can withdraw consent
      at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your account and content for as long as your account is active. If you ask
      us to delete your account, we'll remove your personal data within a reasonable
      time — except limited records we're legally required to keep, such as payment
      history.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can view and update your profile, change or turn off reminders, control what
      the community sees, and unsubscribe from marketing emails using the link in any
      newsletter. To request a copy of your data or to delete your account, email
      <a href="mailto:julia@meibostouch.com">julia@meibostouch.com</a>. Depending on
      where you live, you may have additional rights under laws such as the GDPR or the
      CCPA, and we will honor valid requests.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      We protect your account with hashed passwords, encrypted connections (HTTPS), and
      access controls. No system is perfectly secure, but we take reasonable steps to
      safeguard your information.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The Creative's Garden is intended for adults. It is not directed to children, and
      we do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 16.
    </p>

    <h2>Where your data is processed</h2>
    <p>
      The platform is hosted in the United States. If you access it from elsewhere, your
      information may be transferred to and processed in the United States.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as the platform grows or the law changes. We'll update
      the "last updated" date above, and for significant changes we'll let you know.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about your privacy? Email
      <a href="mailto:julia@meibostouch.com">julia@meibostouch.com</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="legal-footer">
      The Creative's Garden — a content creation course by The Meibos Touch.
    </p>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
